<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gian Lorenzo Bernini</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1598–1680</span> · Also known as Bernini</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gian Lorenzo Bernini was an Italian sculptor and architect, the leading artist of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Working for successive popes, he designed the bronze baldacchino and the great colonnade of St Peter's Square at the Vatican, the Fountain of the Four Rivers in Piazza Navona, and sculptures such as the Ecstasy of Saint Teresa. His work shaped the appearance of papal Rome.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gian-lorenzo-bernini.jpg" alt="Gian Lorenzo Bernini" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gian Lorenzo Bernini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gian_Lorenzo_Bernini,_self-portrait,_c1623.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
